[Observation & Comparison with Problem 2]:
  - Unlike Hub-A, Switch-B performs Backward MAC Learning from source frames.
  - Initial MAC table was empty. As packets flowed, ports Fa0/1, Fa0/2, Fa0/3 were
    associated with the corresponding host MAC addresses.
  - Subsequent unicast frames were selectively switched ONLY to the destination port,
    eliminating collision domains (microsegmentation) and conserving bandwidth.

